cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "heavytails: A Python Library for Heavy-Tailed Probability Distributions"
message: "If you use this library, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ribeiro
    given-names: Diogo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2022-7072"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Media Arts and Design, Technical University of Porto"
    email: dfr@esmad.ipp.pt
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/heavytails"
url: "https://diogoribeiro7.github.io/heavytails"
abstract: >
  heavytails is a Python library implementing heavy-tailed probability
  distributions, built from first principles with NumPy-backed vectorized
  evaluation. The library provides comprehensive support for continuous and
  discrete heavy-tailed distributions, tail index estimation methods, and
  diagnostic utilities for extreme value analysis, risk management, and
  financial modeling.
keywords:
  - heavy tails
  - heavy-tailed distributions
  - probability distributions
  - statistics
  - data science
  - machine learning
  - extreme value theory
  - tail index estimation
  - risk management
  - finance
  - tail risk
  - python
  - simulation
  - teaching
